<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Identifying parameters on a sinusoidal curve</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>
The graph below represents the sinusoidal function \(f(x)\).
</p>

[[jsxgraph height='500px' width='700px']]
  var board = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {
      boundingbox: [-2*Math.PI, 6, 2*Math.PI, -6],
      axis: true,
      showCopyright: false
  });

  var f = board.jc.snippet('{#f#}', true, 'x', true);

  board.create('functiongraph', [f, -2*Math.PI, 2*Math.PI]);
[[/jsxgraph]]

<p>
Determine the following features of the function:
</p>

<ol>
  <li>
    Amplitude:
    [[input:ans1]]
    [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]
  </li>

  <li>
    Period:
    [[input:ans2]]
    [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]
  </li>

  <li>
    Equation of the midline:
    \(y=\) [[input:ans3]]
    [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]
  </li>

  <li>
    Maximum value:
    [[input:ans4]]
    [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]
  </li>

  <li>
    Minimum value:
    [[input:ans5]]
    [[validation:ans5]] [[feedback:prt5]]
  </li>
</ol>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The graph is \(f(x)={@f@}\).</p>
<ul>
<li>Maximum value: \({@ta_max@}\); minimum value: \({@ta_min@}\) (the highest and lowest points of the graph).</li>
<li>Amplitude: half the distance between them, \(\dfrac{ {@ta_max@}-({@ta_min@}) }{2}={@ta_amp@}\).</li>
<li>Midline: halfway between them, \(y=\dfrac{ {@ta_max@}+({@ta_min@}) }{2}={@ta_midline@}\).</li>
<li>Period: the graph repeats every \(\dfrac{2\pi}{ {@B@} }={@ta_period@}\) units.</li>
</ul>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
